    "https://www.mssu.edu/faculty-staff.php": {
      "title": "Information for Faculty and Staff",
      "description": "Information for Faculty and Staff Skip To Top Navigation Skip To Content Skip To Footer Academic Programs Apply Give Visit close search Search MSSU search close Menu Close close Menu About Us About Us MSSU History Accreditations and Memberships Mission Office of the President Academics Academics Program Options Colleges Graduate Programs Online Programs Dual Credit/Dual Enrollment MOSO CAPS Continuing Education Honors Program Global Leaders Global Education Office Law Enforcement Academy Schedule of Classes Admissions Admissions Enrollment Services Campus Tours and Events First Time Students Former Students Transfer Student Graduate Students International Students Tuition and Rates Financial Aid Financial Aid Estimated Cost of Attendance Financial Aid How to Frequently Used Forms Graduate Students Scholarships Types of Financial Aid Veteran Services Life at MSSU Life at MSSU Residence Life Dining Student Activities Recreational Services Student Success Athletics Athletics Lion Athletics Quicklinks Lionet Calendar Course Catalog Email Blackboard News Giving Library Information For Current Students Parents and Family Faculty & Staff Alumni Lionet Calendar Course Catalog Email Blackboard News Giving Library Close close Information for Faculty and Staff Home Information for Faculty and Staff Home In This Section Regardless if you’re a new faculty/staff member, nearing retirement or somewhere in-between, you can benefit from a comprehensive list of tools, sites, and portals to make your job and your life easier. Below, you will find a link to all the essentials—everything you may need as an employee of Missouri Southern, and access to information you may need to pass on to students or fellow faculty and staff. Banner Banner Reports Blackboard Calendar Directory Email Employee Dashboard Financial Services Help Desk Library Lionet Nuventive Pawsitively the Best Sharepoint Emergency Information – Important information about emergency procedures and awareness. Academic Resources Academic Advising – A great academic success resource for students. Catalog - Use this to keep track of all the courses and programs offered for each semester and school year. Center for Integrated Educational Excellence - A hub for faculty development, teaching innovation, and instructional resources. Schedule of Classes – A handy collection of all the important dates and times of semester-relevant testing, class times, financial aid deadlines and more. Academic Calendar – All the important academic dates you and students need to know, such as finals, midterms and campus-wide breaks. Departments and Programs – A guide to all of our departments and programs. Commencement – All you need to know about upcoming graduation ceremonies. Institutional Research – Here you can find information about our university’s effectiveness, research reports, and assessments. Lion Alert – If you believe another student to be at-risk academically, refer him or her so we may provide them with helpful resources as soon as possible. Registrar – This office will help you find student records, transcripts, grades, degree audits, petitions and forms, and more. Faculty Roster and Evaluations FAFSA Information Technology Resources HelpDesk – Give the HelpDesk a call or message if you need help with any technology-related matters or if you need to report a problem with any phones/computers on campus. Banner - Use this link to log onto Banner 9. Banner Reports - Click here for reports on enrollment, budget, purchasing and more. PowerBI Reports - Click here for interactive visual business intelligence reports. WiFi Information – All you need to know about connecting to the university’s internet. Mobile Phone Email Setup - Having difficulty setting up your work email on your phone? This link will help guide you. Acceptable Usage Policy Information – To understand the legal nitty-gritty of using campus materials and internet services. Digital Millenium Copyright Act – View the Digital Millenium Copyright Act Academic Policies Request - Click here for information on academic policy request. Campus Services Reserve a space – Need a room or space for an event? Request it here. Campus Safety – Information about the procedures the university uses to keep campus safe. Facility Services Work Request – Need to request building repairs or maintenance? Create a work request. Fresh Ideas – Click here for nutritional information and dining menus from our campus food distributor. Counseling – If you need to refer a student to counseling services, this is a beneficial resource. Library and Information Services – Our Library is home to a wide range of tools and resources for you to use. The Print Shop - Click here to submit a print request for on-campus printing from our Office Services department. Human Resources Benefits – Wondering what sort of benefits you are entitled to as an MSSU employee? Find out here. Discounts – Working for MSSU allows you to take advantage of discounts with local businesses and national chains. Here’s an exhaustive list of places to use your discount. Travel & reimbursement tool - Use this tool if you've traveled for work and would like reimbursement for expenses. Faculty handbook - A composite guide of policies, procedures and university expectations for all faculty. Staff handbook - A composite guide of policies, procedures and university expectations for all staff members. Student handbook - All the legalities and details of campus policy, dress code and more for students. Training Resources - A resource for you to use for training new-hires, student workers and colleagues. Policy library – A comprehensive list of our university’s policies and procedures. Job opportunities – We’re almost always looking to add new Lions to our Pride. Search open employment options here. Getting Around Campus Maps – Not sure where something is on campus? Use this digital resource. Parking – All you need to know about parking regulations and guidelines on campus. Health and Safety Rave alert – Enter your information here to be alerted in the event of an emergency or incident on-campus. WIP – Learn about our Wellness Incentive Program, which rewards faculty and staff for taking advantage of wellness opportunities on campus. Cigna – Keep up-to-date with information from our insurance provider, Cigna. Employee Organizations Staff Senate – Information about our Staff Senate including how you can get involved. Faculty Senate - Information about our Faculty Senate including how you can get involved. Board of Governors – Information about our university’s governing body. Empowering U Dashboard – View the Empowering U dashboard. Pawsitively the Best – View or submit a PAWsitively the Best review. Keeping up with MOSO Registered Social Media – Follow MOSO on our all platforms to stay up-to-date and show your Lion Pride. MOSO Minute – Our site for news and press releases targeted specifically to faculty and staff. Crossroads – Our alumni-focused magazine filled with updates and stories about campus, alumni, current students, and faculty/staff achievements. New Hires Get your Lion Card – Your Lion Card is your faculty/staff ID. We're All Lions Here You Can Be One, Too Being a Lion means having a family--a Pride--to call on for academic, career and personal support. Schedule a Tour 3950 E. Newman Road Joplin MO 64801 (866) 818-6778 info@mssu.edu Important Accessibility Statement Accreditation Calendar of Events Emergency Management Plan Privacy Policy Request More Information Social Media Hub University Police Resources Apply Online Consumer Information Contact Employment Map Title IX Information Virtual Tour WIOA © Copyright 2024"
    },
