      "description": "MSSU - Open Positions Skip To Top Navigation Skip To Content Skip To Footer Academic Programs Apply Give Visit close search Search MSSU search close Menu Close close Menu About Us About Us MSSU History Accreditations and Memberships Mission Office of the President Academics Academics Program Options Colleges Graduate Programs Online Programs Dual Credit/Dual Enrollment MOSO CAPS Continuing Education Honors Program Global Leaders Global Education Office Law Enforcement Academy Schedule of Classes Admissions Admissions Enrollment Services Campus Tours and Events First Time Students Former Students Transfer Student Graduate Students International Students Tuition and Rates Financial Aid Financial Aid Estimated Cost of Attendance Financial Aid How to Frequently Used Forms Graduate Students Scholarships Types of Financial Aid Veteran Services Life at MSSU Life at MSSU Residence Life Dining Student Activities Recreational Services Student Success Athletics Athletics Lion Athletics Quicklinks Lionet Calendar Course Catalog Email Blackboard News Giving Library Information For Current Students Parents and Family Faculty & Staff Alumni Lionet Calendar Course Catalog Email Blackboard News Giving Library Close close Current Open Positions Home Current Open Positions Human Resources In This Section Human Resources Staff Equal Employment Opportunity Compliance Employee Benefits Applicant Portal Current Open Positions Payroll Department Employment Mandates Welcome to MSSU Missouri Southern is a four-year public university serving over 4,200 students across more than 140 undergraduate and graduate programs. We foster a campus culture rooted in connection through a supportive learning environment for students and engaging educational opportunities for our community. MSSU’s mission to prepare students who Explore Boldly, Care Deeply, and Impact Globally is reflected through three defining pillars: Immersive Learning Experiences, Health and Life Sciences, and Global Education. This unique purpose empowers tomorrow’s leaders to serve and innovate with intention. Become a Lion and enjoy MSSU benefits offered to eligible positions : Health & Wellness 3 Medical Plans Dental & Vision Coverage Life Insurance Flexible Spending Account Employee Assistance Program Willcoxon Health Center (on campus) REC Center Membership (employee & family) Pet Insurance Wellness Incentive Program Financial & Retirement Tuition Discount MOSERS Retirement Plan 403(b) or 457(b) Options TIAA/CURP (Faculty) Flexible Spending Account Voluntary Life Insurance Short-Term & Long-Term Disability Public Service Loan Forgiveness Time Off & Flexibility Vacation, Sick & Bereavement Leave 15 Paid Holidays Extra paid time off during Spring/Fall Break, Thanksgiving and Winter Break Paid Parental Leave Summer Hours (Mon-Thurs) Flexible Work Opportunities About Joplin MSSU is in Joplin, MO—the Crossroads of America—and serves as a commercial hub for the four states. With a variety of cuisine selections, scenic hiking trails, concerts, art exhibits, professional sports, and rich cultural events in the Historic Downtown District, you’ll always have something here to explore. Our campus is the perfect place to call your professional home. Your browser does not support iframes please go to The Standalone Job Finder Tool Equal Opportunity Employer MSSU is committed to promoting an equal employment opportunity workplace. Equal opportunity is and shall be provided for all employees and applicants for employment on the basis of their demonstrated ability and competence without discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, age, national origin, genetic information (GINA), physical or mental disability, pregnancy, sexual orientation, gender identity, marital status, familial status, ancestry, military and/or veteran status, and/or any other status protected by applicable Federal, state or local law. Annual Security Report MSSU is committed to providing a safe campus for students, faculty, and staff. Our annual campus security report lists campus crimes and statistics for the campus and public areas around campus for the last three years, in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. We're All Lions Here You Can Be One, Too Being a Lion means having a family--a Pride--to call on for academic, career and personal support. Schedule a Tour 3950 E. Newman Road Joplin MO 64801 (866) 818-6778 info@mssu.edu Important Accessibility Statement Accreditation Calendar of Events Emergency Management Plan Privacy Policy Request More Information Social Media Hub University Police Resources Apply Online Consumer Information Contact Employment Map Title IX Information Virtual Tour WIOA © Copyright 2024"
